# Caddy in front of the relay, for the one job it is here to do: get a real
# HTTPS certificate automatically, so the desktop app is not talking to your
# server in the clear.
#
# Copy this to "Caddyfile" (no extension) and put your own hostname on the
# first line. Caddy fetches and renews the certificate by itself; there is
# nothing else to configure and no certificate file to manage.
#
# You only need this if you are exposing the relay to the internet. If the
# relay is staying on your own machine or your own network, skip Caddy
# entirely and point the app at http://localhost:8080, or at the machine's
# local address like http://192.168.1.20:8080 — see README.md, "Do I need a
# domain? Almost certainly not".

your-name-here.duckdns.org {
    reverse_proxy localhost:8080
}
